# Conclusion

The analysis explored the relationship between Spotify audio features and track popularity using multiple modeling approaches.

A multiple linear regression model initially captured modest linear relationships between audio features and popularity. A regression tree was fitted to detect nonlinear relationships and feature interactions, offering interpretability through split thresholds. Finally, a Random Forest model, tuned using cross-validation, achieved a lower RMSE on the test set compared to the linear regression model, indicating superior predictive performance by accounting for complex feature interactions.

Nevertheless, the models explain only a fraction of the variability in track popularity, suggesting that external factors like artist reputation, playlist placement, and social media influence remain substantial determinants of success.

